`readOwnPath(record, path)` traverses only own properties. `record` must be a non-null object or function. `path` must be a nonempty array of nonempty strings; malformed arguments throw `TypeError`. Return `{ found: true, value }` when every segment exists as an own property, including when the final value is `undefined`. Return `{ found: false, value: undefined }` when a segment is absent or traversal would continue through `null` or a primitive. An empty-string key is invalid. Preserve path order and do not mutate or copy the record, path, or result value.

